  "problem": "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14057748/assets/21e310adffbad6309176ea26549e0e43efe3d8e3d7f2f0b018902be16781802d.png)\n\nThe graph of the function $y=g(x)$ is shown above. Approximate ${g}^{\u2032}(x)$ at the point $x=1.5$ using a forward difference approximation with step size $h=1.$",
  "worked_solution": "We use the forward difference approximation\n\n$$\n{g}^{\u2032}(x)\u2248\\frac{g(x+h)-g(x)}{h}\n$$\n\n \nat the point $x=1.5.$ Applying the above formula with $x=1.5$ and $h=1$ gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{g}^{\u2032}(1.5) & \u2248\\frac{g(1.5+1)-g(1.5)}{1} \\\\  & =\\frac{g(2.5)-g(1.5)}{1} \\\\  & =4-2 \\\\  & =2.\\end{aligned}\n$$",
